message: "If you use this project in your research, please cite it using the following metadata and cite the original datasets separately."
title: "Nigeria's Climate Reality: What Is Changing, Who Is Affected, and Why It Matters"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Obasi-Uzoma"
    given-names: "Blessing Chinanuekpere"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
url: "https://storymaps.arcgis.com/stories/1354cc766aad4f75aa19a2493a844a02"
abstract: >-
  An exploratory geospatial research and visualisation project examining
  long-term temperature trends, rainfall variability, modelled river-flood
  hazard, and estimated population distribution across Nigeria using
  climate datasets, gridded population data, and geographic information
  systems. The project communicates spatial patterns and methodological
  limitations through an interactive ArcGIS StoryMap.
keywords:
  - Nigeria
  - Climate change
  - Geospatial analysis
  - GIS
  - Temperature trends
  - Rainfall variability
  - Flood hazard
  - Population distribution
  - Climate data
  - ArcGIS StoryMaps

